From 394b2c2e78116d775b5cd610bc7471e8b2f1fbd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John <john.de.kroon@cyberant.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:12:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] client: BADGE, LF graph buffers of 64K samples (were
 128K)

With 128K samples the LF demodulators' per-try buffers (MAX_GRAPH_TRACE_LEN
bytes and ints: 128 KB and 512 KB, calloc'd and freed for every
modulation and clock tried) ran the badge's user pool out: from the app a
T55xx detect got the app stopped by apprun (pool free 1.1 MB, largest
598 KB), or hung the badge until the watchdog; lf t55xx chk did so from a
shell too (2026-10-31, a T5577). The RDV4 delivers at most ~40 KB of
samples, so 64K is enough; every use of the constant is a bound (MIN or a
comparison) or a buffer of that size. Halves those buffers and frees
512 KB of the two static ones.

Tested: built for the badge; on the badge see the next test round.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 client/src/graph.h | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/client/src/graph.h b/client/src/graph.h
index 939858527..3affeee21 100644
--- a/client/src/graph.h
+++ b/client/src/graph.h
@@ -69,10 +69,13 @@ size_t restore_buffer8(buffer_savestate_t saveState, uint8_t *dest);
 
 // The badge (BADGE build) has little RAM: three int32 buffers of 40000*32
 // samples are 15 MB. Its Proxmark3 RDV4 delivers at most ~40 KB of samples
-// (BigBuf), so 128K samples per buffer is plenty there.
+// (BigBuf), so 64K samples per buffer is enough there. 128K was too much:
+// the LF demodulators calloc and free buffers of this many bytes and ints
+// for every try, and with 128K a T55xx detect or password check ran the
+// user pool out (2026-10-31); the two static buffers are 256 KB each now.
 #ifndef MAX_GRAPH_TRACE_LEN
 #ifdef BADGE
-#define MAX_GRAPH_TRACE_LEN (128 * 1024)
+#define MAX_GRAPH_TRACE_LEN (64 * 1024)
 #else
 #define MAX_GRAPH_TRACE_LEN (40000 * 32)
 #endif
